{
  "name": "neverball-mapc",
  "title": "NEVERBALL's map compiler, mapc (Robert Kooima and the Neverball team; 1.6.0, 2014): .map levels to .sol",
  "dir": "corpus/neverball-1.6.0",
  "fetch": "curl -sL https://neverball.org/neverball-1.6.0.tar.gz | tar -xz -C corpus (sha256 73fe63cc...a88fa0; SHA-512 and size as NetBSD pkgsrc's games/neverball/distinfo); libpng 1.6.16 (https://download.sourceforge.net/libpng/libpng-1.6.16.tar.gz, sha256 02f96b6b...2073ad); libjpeg 6b and zlib 1.1.3 as for chromium-bsu",
  "_build": "The Makefile's MAPC_OBJS with ENABLE_FS=stdio (its own switch: share/fs_stdio.c instead of PhysicsFS), and its flags: -std=c99, -DNDEBUG (a release build), CONFIG_USER/CONFIG_DATA/CONFIG_LOCALE, ENABLE_NLS=0, and -Umain on mapc as the Makefile passes it. share/version.h is what scripts/version.sh writes for a release build (version.in.h with 1.6.0), in corpus/neverball-1.6.0-generated. libpng is scripts/makefile.linux's OBJS over its own scripts/pnglibconf.h.prebuilt (the documented build without configure), in corpus/libpng-1.6.16-generated; libjpeg is the jpeg-6b objects chromium-bsu already uses, over zlib 1.1.3.",
  "units": {
    "list": [
      "share/vec3.c",
      "share/base_image.c",
      "share/solid_base.c",
      "share/binary.c",
      "share/base_config.c",
      "share/common.c",
      "share/fs_common.c",
      "share/fs_png.c",
